kind: llman.sdd.delta
ops[2]{op,req_id,title,statement,from,to,name}:
  add_requirement,tui62,"list-selection-atom","The TUI MUST provide a ListSelection component (src/app/tui/components/list_selection.rs) as a reusable interaction atom: a pure logic state machine (Vec<T> plus selected_index plus page_size, with move_up/move_down/confirm/cancel and wrap-around) separate from its render function, so that picker-style components (approval overlay, model selector, command popup) can reuse the state machine without rewriting list rendering. Evidence: kimi-code SearchableList (utils/searchable-list.ts) is a render-free pure state machine reused by three pickers; codex ScrollState plus selection_popup_common shared row rendering; pi SelectList centered scroll window.",null,null,null
  add_requirement,tui63,"approval-overlay-composes-list","The TUI MUST provide an ApprovalOverlay component that consumes a UI-only ApprovalRequest (call_id, tool_name, summary) translated from XyEvent::ToolApprovalRequired at a single seam in app.rs, and MUST compose ListSelection (not rewrite list rendering) for its allow/deny/view-details choices; the approval decision MUST be written back through the Driver trait (e.g. approve_tool), not by reaching into agent internals, preserving the tui4 reuse contract. Evidence: codex ApprovalOverlay composes ListSelectionView and delegates rendering (approval_overlay.rs:607); it builds SelectionItem list from ApprovalRequest via build_options and sends decisions via AppEventSender.",null,null,null
op_scenarios[4]{req_id,id,given,when,then}:
  tui62,"state-machine-is-pure",the ListSelection source is inspected,the state machine and render function are checked,"the state machine has no rendering dependency (no Buffer/Frame/Style) and the render function is separate, both independently testable via TestBackend"
  tui62,"wrap-around",a ListSelection with the last item selected,move_down is invoked,selection wraps to the first item
  tui63,"approval-translates-xyevent","an XyEvent::ToolApprovalRequired arrives during a turn",app.rs handles the event,"it translates to a UI-only ApprovalRequest and the ApprovalOverlay consumes that type (the overlay source does not match on XyEvent variants)"
  tui63,"approval-via-driver",the user selects allow in the ApprovalOverlay,the decision is applied,"it is written back through a Driver trait method (not a direct agent call), so InProcessDriver and RemoteDriver both carry it"
